{"name":"Milk Punch","hex":"#fff4d3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"milk punch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hot Irish drink, scáiltín, made from equal amounts of hot whiskey and milk.","A cold beverage of milk, bourbon, sugar, and vanilla extract, common in New Orleans."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/milk_punch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Milk punch","blocks":[{"text":"Milk punch is a milk-based brandy or bourbon beverage. It consists of milk, the spirit, sugar, and vanilla extract. It is served cold and usually has nutmeg sprinkled on top. Milk punch may be clarified through the addition of ingredients which cause the milk to curdle, so that the solids contributing to the beverage's opacity may be strained out."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Glass_of_eggnog.jpg/330px-Glass_of_eggnog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milk_punch","wikidata":"Q6858052"},{"title":"Punch (monkey)","blocks":[{"text":"Punch-kun , or simply Punch, sometimes also referred to as Punch Monkey, is a baby Japanese macaque, or snow monkey, at the Ichikawa City Zoo in Japan. He gained viral attention on social media for his attachment to a large orangutan stuffed toy. Punch's internet popularity led to a surge in visitors to the zoo starting in February 2026."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Punch_the_Monkey_Ichikawa_City_Zoo_2026_2.png/330px-Punch_the_Monkey_Ichikawa_City_Zoo_2026_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punch_(monkey)","wikidata":"Q138358320"},{"title":"Punch (drink)","blocks":[{"text":"The term punch refers to a wide assortment of drinks, both alcoholic and non-alcoholic, generally containing fruits or fruit juice. The drink was introduced from the Indian subcontinent to England by employees of the East India Company in the late 17th century. Punch is usually served at parties in large, wide bowls, known as punch bowls."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Bowle_Steinhude_2009_20090822_3.JPG/330px-Bowle_Steinhude_2009_20090822_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punch_(drink)","wikidata":"Q1121224"},{"title":"Milk","blocks":[{"text":"Milk is usually a white liquid food produced by the mammary glands of lactating mammals. It is the primary source of nutrition for young mammals before they are able to digest solid food. Milk contains many nutrients, including calcium and protein, as well as lactose and saturated fat; the enzyme lactase is needed to break down lactose. Immune factors and immune-modulating components in milk contribute to milk immunity. The first milk, which is called colostrum, contains antibodies and immune-modulating components that strengthen the immune system against many diseases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg/330px-Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milk","wikidata":"Q8495"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Clarified_milk_punches_in_tasting_glasses.jpg/500px-Clarified_milk_punches_in_tasting_glasses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Clarified_milk_punches_in_tasting_glasses.jpg/500px-Clarified_milk_punches_in_tasting_glasses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two clarified milk punches served in tasting glasses. The one on the left is made from Batavia arrack, ruby port, black tea, lemon juice, milk, and sugar; the one on the right is made from brandy infused with orange and lemon peels, orange and lemon juices, milk, and sugar. Rather than the traditional use of bovine milk, oat milk was used in both beverages so that they would be suitable for consumption by vegans.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClarified_milk_punches_in_tasting_glasses.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Punch_the_Monkey_Ichikawa_City_Zoo_2026_9.png/500px-Punch_the_Monkey_Ichikawa_City_Zoo_2026_9.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Punch_the_Monkey_Ichikawa_City_Zoo_2026_9.png/1280px-Punch_the_Monkey_Ichikawa_City_Zoo_2026_9.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Punch_the_Monkey_Ichikawa_City_Zoo_2026_9.png/500px-Punch_the_Monkey_Ichikawa_City_Zoo_2026_9.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Punch with his orangutan stuffed toy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APunch_the_Monkey_Ichikawa_City_Zoo_2026_9.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Southern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg/500px-Southern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Southern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg/1280px-Southern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Southern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg/500px-Southern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Southern Bourbon Punch","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASouthern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Bowle.JPG/500px-Bowle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thum